# II. CHORALE, FAR OFF  b35-45  (E-flat major, 4/4)
# Four players only: horn 1 (soprano), horn 2 (alto), trombone 1 (tenor),
# bass trombone (bass) - the first sound of the trombones in the piece.
# Pianissimo, as if from another room.  The G of the sarabande's last
# chord becomes the third of E-flat: no modulation, just a change of
# light.  The chorale's head (g d eb bb) is the sarabande's head
# (c g ab eb) in the major.
# Between the phrases a single string voice answers with the
# sarabande's head IN THE MINOR, each a step further from the dark:
#   b37 solo viola (b-flat minor shadow of the V chord),
#   b40 solo cello (g minor shadow of the G-major half cadence),
#   b43 the first violins: c g a-flat ... and the horn's e-flat 5 that
#        opens the last phrase completes the head - the minor question
#        and the major answer become one line.
# Phrase ends carry fermatas; their length is written into the tempo map.

